title: Conductor revival Phase 0 — ATRIUM keystone spike built + release-verified
summary: Phase 0 of the Conductor revival is implemented and builds clean in release. Conductor now spawns a headless `claude -p` over stream-json (bidirectional), decodes the NDJSON event stream off-main into typed Swift, projects it into an observable conversation model, and renders it in a custom ATRIUM SwiftUI thread (custom UI, not terminal-scraping) launchable from the menu bar. Mechanism was empirically proven first (one-shot + tool-event + bidirectional-stdin tests against the real CLI). 12 files created, 2 modified; swift build -c release → Build complete, exit 0. Live visual round-trip pending founder launch (GUI).
