learnings:
  - 'Confirmed claude -p stream-json event shapes empirically: system/init carries session_id (resume handle); assistant.message.content is heterogeneous blocks (text / thinking / tool_use{id,name,input}); tool RESULTS arrive as a separate type:user event with a tool_result block keyed by tool_use_id; result event carries total_cost_usd + usage. Bidirectional stdin works: write {type:user,message:{role:user,content:[{type:text,text}]}}\n, keep stdin open, same session_id continues.'
  - 'Two Swift-6 risks were the real implementation hazards: (1) readabilityHandler is @Sendable/off-main — must NOT touch @Published; pattern is nonisolated ingest → Sendable LineFramer → Task{@MainActor} apply. (2) LineFramer must accumulate Data (not String), split on 0x0A, retain trailing partial fragment, skip undecodable lines, flush on EOF. Both handled.'
  - Conductor already had AgentProcessManager (headless claude spawn, raw stdout lines) — the spike built ClaudeStreamSession BESIDE it (structured stream-json) rather than mutating the working Symphony spawn path.
