body: |-
  Spike scope (deliberately narrow, single-owner): hardcoded to the a-paradigm repo path + a fixed opening prompt, launched from an AppDelegate menu item "Open ATRIUM Spike…" into a standalone 720x720 window. Uses --dangerously-skip-permissions to avoid permission round-trips (Phase 1 must revisit). Renders: user turns (cool-blue right lane), agent turns (ink, amber streaming caret), tool_use as collapsible violet chips that resolve running→✓/✕, footer with model·session_id·tokens·$cost. thinking blocks skipped; unknown event types tolerated.

  Verify (founder, GUI): cd packages/conductor && swift build -c release && launch Conductor → menu bar → "Open ATRIUM Spike…". Expect the auto-sent opening turn to stream in with a tool chip (dir listing) resolving, then reply via the composer to continue the same session.

  Next (Phase 1): parameterize projectPath/role, resume via captured session_id, render thinking + token-level partial streaming (include-partial-messages), real permission round-trip (drop skip-permissions), integrate into the spine/workspace rather than a standalone window. Builder agentId a8865cf5f8de8d43e; architect a5b9392cd39e64448; Mika (ATRIUM) a9816c3a468257205.
